	"nodes":[
		{"id":"cb19bdc0cf32095e","type":"text","text":"## Passive Investment Management\n\n#### Core Objective\n\nDesigned to match the risk and return performance of a specified benchmark index like the S&P 500.\n\n#### Implementation Methods\n\n* **Full Replication**: Holding **every security** in the **benchmark** in exact **proportion** to its **weighting**.\n* **Sampling/Tracking**: Holding a **representative** **subset** of benchmark securities when full replication is costly/illiquid.\n\n#### Key Metric & Risk\n\nFocuses on minimising tracking error (standard deviation of the difference between portfolio and benchmark returns). Investor accepts systematic risk of the underlying market.\n\n#### Costs & Efficiency Belief\n\nOperates on the premise that markets are informationally efficient (security prices reflect available information). Lower management fees and transaction costs).\n\n#### Asset Class Suitability\n\nWell suited for broad liquid public markets such as major stock and bond indices.","x":-880,"y":-880,"width":840,"height":720},
		{"id":"5f5cad10f256f1cf","type":"text","text":"## Passive and Active Management\n\n","x":203,"y":-230,"width":420,"height":70},
		{"id":"9c2d2aef794058ba","type":"file","file":"Attachments/Pasted image 20261112090212.png","x":40,"y":-952,"width":746,"height":352},
		{"id":"1bffcaaac1d9ce97","type":"text","text":"## Active Investment Management\n\n#### Core Objective\n\nAttempts to add value by selecting investments expected to outperform a specified benchmark.\n\n#### Implementation Methods\n\n* Security Selection & Market Timing: Buying assets expected to outperform, selling/avoiding those expected to underperform. Tactical asset allocation to exploit short term market shifts.\n* Analytical approaches: Utilising fundamental analysis (evaluating business models and intrinsic value), technical/behavioural analysis or quantitative modelling. [[Market Inefficiencies.canvas]]\n\n#### Key Metric & Risk\n\nIncurs a higher tracking error (active risk) and assumes specific risk to generate alpha (consistent outperformance due to manager skill)\n\n#### Costs & Efficiency Belief\n\nOperates on the premise that markets contain inefficiencies or mis-pricings that can be exploited. Requires skilled analysts, advanced technology and frequent trading resulting in higher management fees and transaction costs. Outperformance must be large enough to cover these extra costs to yield higher net returns.\n\n#### Asset Class Suitability\n\nBest suited for less efficient or privately traded asset classes such as small cap equities, emerging markets, real estate, private equity and venture capital.","x":960,"y":-880,"width":960,"height":800}
	],
